  "worked_solution": "If we have a data set that consists of the points ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},\u2026,{x}_{n},$ then the variance can be computed as\n\n$$\n{\\sigma }^{2}=\\overset{\u2015}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{\u2015}{x})^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{\u2015}{x}$ is the mean of the data set and $\\overset{\u2015}{{x}^{2}}$ is the mean of the squares of the points in the data set.\n\nFirst, let's compute $\\overset{\u2015}{x}.$ There are $n=6$ points in our data set, so the mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\u2015}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot (-18-11-8+4+6-3) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot (-30) \\\\  & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\overset{\u2015}{{x}^{2}}.$ Computing the mean of the squares of the points in the data set, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\u2015}{{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot ((-18)^{2}+(-11)^{2}+(-8)^{2}+{4}^{2}+{6}^{2}+(-3)^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot (324+121+64+16+36+9) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot 570 \\\\  & =\\frac{570}{6} \\\\  & =95.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =\\overset{\u2015}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{\u2015}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =95-{(-5)}^{2} \\\\  & =95-25 \\\\  & =70.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
